-- Payload-free enums stored in discovery rows.
enum PackageKind:
	NativePackage
	SourcePackage


---
Where a module's source came from.
---
enum ModuleOriginKind:
	StdlibModule
	PackageModule
	UserModule


---
How discovery reached a module: named as a root, or only through imports.
---
enum ModuleReach:
	RootModule
	ImportedModule


---
The syntax of an import request, before any module exists. A bare path
(`heap`, `lib/source`) may resolve to a standard-library module, a source
package or a local file, in the order the source provider defines; a
relative path starts with `./` or `../`; a native package path starts with
`pkg/`. The design sketch called the bare form a "stdlib request"; the syntax
does not decide that, the provider does.
---
enum ImportRequestKind:
	BareModuleRequest
	RelativeModuleRequest
	NativePackageRequest


---
What a definition row declares. Members (fields, variants, trait and impl
methods) link to their owner with a `MemberRow`; a `LocalFunctionDefinition`
is a function declared inside a body, reached from its `LocalFunctionNode`.
---
enum DefinitionKind:
	FunctionDefinition
	RecordDefinition
	StructDefinition
	UnionDefinition
	EnumDefinition
	BuiltinTypeDefinition
	ResourceTypeDefinition
	TypeAliasDefinition
	OpaqueTypeDefinition
	TraitDefinition
	ImplDefinition
	ConstantDefinition
	MutableGlobalDefinition
	ForeignFunctionDefinition
	FieldDefinition
	VariantDefinition
	TraitMethodDefinition
	ImplMethodDefinition
	LocalFunctionDefinition


enum Visibility:
	PublicVisibility
	PrivateVisibility


---
A type parameter's kind: a type (`T`), a dimension (`#N`), or the wildcard
dimension `#_`, whose name column holds `_`.
---
enum TypeParameterKind:
	TypeParameter
	DimensionParameter
	WildcardDimensionParameter


enum Purity:
	PureFunction
	ImpureFunction


---
How a parameter binds its argument: `name` (or `_: Type`), `_`, or a tuple
`(a, b)`.
---
enum ParameterBinder:
	NamedParameterBinder
	WildcardParameterBinder
	TupleParameterBinder


---
The function annotations the language defines (`@tail_recursive`, ...).
---
enum FunctionAnnotation:
	TailRecursiveAnnotation
	NoCopyAnnotation
	DebugOnlyAnnotation
	ResourceResultOrdinaryAnnotation


---
The syntactic form of a node. The meaning of a node's `payload` and the order
of its children are fixed by its kind, and `node_payload_reference` says which
table the payload indexes. Expressions, statements, patterns and written types
share the node table; `...TypeNode` kinds appear only where a type was written
and `...PatternNode` kinds only where a pattern was. Kinds without a payload
store `NO_NODE_PAYLOAD` there. A child documented as "when written" is present
only when the source wrote it; it is recognized by its kind (a type child has a
`...TypeNode` kind), never by position alone.

- `IdentifierNode`: A name used as a value. payload: the `NameId`; no children.
- `IntegerLiteralNode`: payload: the `LiteralId` of the digits; no children.
- `FloatLiteralNode`: payload: the `LiteralId` of the digits and dot; no children.
- `StringLiteralNode`: A `"..."` string. payload: the `LiteralId` of the text after escapes; no children.
- `RawStringLiteralNode`: A `raw"..."` string. payload: the `LiteralId` of the text as written; no children.
- `PipeStringLiteralNode`: A pipe string. payload: the `LiteralId` of the joined lines; no children.
- `RawPipeStringLiteralNode`: A raw pipe string. payload: the `LiteralId` of the joined lines as written; no children.
- `InterpolatedStringNode`: A string with `${...}` holes. No payload; children: `InterpolationTextNode` pieces and hole expressions in source order (a piece before, between and after holes when it is non-empty).
- `InterpolationTextNode`: The decoded text of an interpolated string between holes. payload: the `LiteralId` of the text; no children.
- `InterpolatedPipeStringNode`: A pipe string with holes; children as `InterpolatedStringNode`.
- `TrueLiteralNode`: `True`; no payload or children.
- `FalseLiteralNode`: `False`; no payload or children.
- `CharLiteralNode`: payload: the codepoint; no children.
- `NegateNode`: `-x`. child: the operand.
- `NotNode`: `not x`. child: the operand.
- `DetachNode`: `detach x`. child: the operand.
- `AddNode`: `+`. children: the left and right operands.
- `SubtractNode`: `-`. children: the left and right operands.
- `MultiplyNode`: `*`. children: the left and right operands.
- `DivideNode`: `/`. children: the left and right operands.
- `ModuloNode`: `%`. children: the left and right operands.
- `EqualNode`: `==`. children: the left and right operands.
- `NotEqualNode`: `!=`. children: the left and right operands.
- `LessNode`: `<`. children: the left and right operands.
- `LessEqualNode`: `<=`. children: the left and right operands.
- `GreaterNode`: `>`. children: the left and right operands.
- `GreaterEqualNode`: `>=`. children: the left and right operands.
- `AndNode`: `and`. children: the left and right operands.
- `OrNode`: `or`. children: the left and right operands.
- `RangeNode`: `a..b`. children: the start and the end.
- `CallNode`: children: the callee, then the arguments in order.
- `FieldAccessNode`: `x.f`. payload: the `NameId` of the field; child: the receiver.
- `SubscriptNode`: `x[i, ...]`. children: the target, then the indices.
- `ListLiteralNode`: `[a, b]`. children: the items.
- `TupleNode`: `(a, b)`. children: the items.
- `VectorLiteralNode`: `{a, b}`. children: the items.
- `RecordLiteralNode`: `{f = v, ...}`. children: one `RecordFieldNode` per field.
- `RecordUpdateNode`: `{r | f = v}`. children: the record, then one `RecordFieldNode` per field.
- `RecordFieldNode`: `f = v` in a record literal or update. payload: the `NameId` of the field; child: the value.
- `DictLiteralNode`: `{k => v, ...}`. children: one `DictEntryNode` per entry.
- `DictEntryNode`: children: the key, then the value.
- `IntoOpaqueNode`: `into_opaque T(x)`. children: the type, then the value.
- `FromOpaqueNode`: `from_opaque T(x)`. children: the type, then the value.
- `BlockNode`: An indented block. children: its statements in order; the last is its value. Empty only in recovery, where a diagnostic row reports the missing block.
- `IfNode`: children: the condition, the then block, and the else branch (a block or an `IfNode`) when written.
- `MatchNode`: children: the scrutinee, then one `MatchCaseNode` per case.
- `MatchCaseNode`: children: the pattern, then the body.
- `SelectNode`: children: the arms.
- `SelectReceiveArmNode`: `name from channel:`. payload: the `NameId` of the binder; children: the channel, then the body.
- `SelectSealedArmNode`: `sealed channel:`. children: the channel, then the body.
- `SelectAfterArmNode`: `_ after timeout:`. children: the timeout, then the body.
- `WithNode`: children: the binding (`WithBindingNode` or `WithTryBindingNode`), then the body.
- `WithBindingNode`: `name [: T] = value`. payload: the `NameId`; children: the type when written, then the value.
- `WithTryBindingNode`: `name [: T] ?= value [on e => mapped]`. payload: the `NameId`; children: the type when written, the value, then a `WithErrorMapNode` when written.
- `WithErrorMapNode`: `on e => value`. payload: the `NameId` of the error binder; child: the value.
- `DebugBlockNode`: `debug:` block. child: the body.
- `LambdaNode`: `func(params) [-> R]: body`. children: one `LambdaParameterNode` per parameter, the return type when written, then the body.
- `PureLambdaNode`: A `pure func(...)` lambda; children as `LambdaNode`.
- `LambdaParameterNode`: payload: the `NameId`; child: the type when written.
- `LocalFunctionNode`: A function declared in a body. payload: the `DefinitionId` of its `LocalFunctionDefinition` row, which carries its signature and body rows; no children.
- `WhileNode`: children: the condition, then the body.
- `ForNode`: children: the binder (`LoopBinderNode` or `TupleLoopBinderNode`), the iterable, then the body.
- `LoopBinderNode`: payload: the `NameId` of the loop variable; no children.
- `TupleLoopBinderNode`: `(a, b)` loop variables. children: one `LoopBinderNode` per name.
- `ConcurrentForNode`: `for x in xs concurrently(...)`. children: the `LoopBinderNode`, the iterable, one `ConcurrentParameterNode` per parameter, then the body.
- `ConcurrentBlockNode`: `concurrent[(...)]:`. children: one `ConcurrentParameterNode` per parameter, then the body.
- `ConcurrentParameterNode`: `name: value`. payload: the `NameId`; child: the value.
- `BreakNode`: `break`; no payload or children.
- `ContinueNode`: `continue`; no payload or children.
- `VoidNode`: `void`, `()` or `_` as a value; no payload or children.
- `BuiltinNode`: A bare `builtin` body; no payload or children.
- `NamedBuiltinNode`: `builtin("name")`. payload: the `LiteralId` of the name; no children.
- `MissingExpressionNode`: Where an expression or statement could not be parsed; a diagnostic row reports it. children: the parts that did parse, if any.
- `VarDeclarationNode`: `var name [: T] = value`. payload: the `NameId`; children: the type when written, then the value.
- `TypedBindingNode`: `name: T = value`. payload: the `NameId`; children: the type, then the value.
- `AssignmentNode`: `name = value`, as a statement or as a named argument inside a `CallNode`'s arguments. payload: the `NameId`; child: the value.
- `QuestionBindNode`: `name [: T] ?= value`. payload: the `NameId`; children: the type when written, then the value.
- `AddAssignNode`: `name += value`. payload: the `NameId`; child: the value.
- `SubtractAssignNode`: `name -= value`; as `AddAssignNode`.
- `MultiplyAssignNode`: `name *= value`; as `AddAssignNode`.
- `DivideAssignNode`: `name /= value`; as `AddAssignNode`.
- `SubscriptAssignmentNode`: `x[i] = value`. children: the `SubscriptNode`, then the value.
- `TupleDestructureNode`: `(a, b) = value`. children: one `DestructureBinderNode` per name, then the value.
- `DestructureBinderNode`: payload: the `NameId`; no children.
- `WildcardPatternNode`: `_`; no payload or children.
- `NamePatternNode`: payload: the `NameId` bound or matched; no children.
- `IntegerPatternNode`: payload: the `LiteralId` of the digits; no children.
- `NegativeIntegerPatternNode`: `-3`. payload: the `LiteralId` of the digits after `-`; no children.
- `FloatPatternNode`: payload: the `LiteralId` of the digits; no children.
- `NegativeFloatPatternNode`: payload: the `LiteralId` of the digits after `-`; no children.
- `StringPatternNode`: payload: the `LiteralId` of the string's text; no children.
- `CharPatternNode`: payload: the codepoint; no children.
- `TruePatternNode`: `True`; no payload or children.
- `FalsePatternNode`: `False`; no payload or children.
- `ConstructorPatternNode`: `Name(p, ...)`. payload: the `NameId` of the constructor; children: the argument patterns.
- `QualifiedConstructorPatternNode`: `Type.Name[(p, ...)]`. payload: the `NameId` of the constructor; children: one `PatternQualifierNode`, then the argument patterns.
- `PatternQualifierNode`: payload: the `NameId` of the qualifying type; no children.
- `TuplePatternNode`: children: the element patterns.
- `ListPatternNode`: `[p, ..., ...rest]`. children: the element patterns, then a `ListSpreadNameNode` or `ListSpreadWildcardNode` when written.
- `ListSpreadNameNode`: `...rest`. payload: the `NameId`; no children.
- `ListSpreadWildcardNode`: `..._`; no payload or children.
- `OrPatternNode`: `p | q`. children: the alternatives.
- `MissingPatternNode`: Where a pattern was required and none was written; a diagnostic row reports it. No payload or children.
- `NamedTypeNode`: A named type (`Int`, `List[T]`, `Self`, `()` as `Void`). payload: the `NameId` of the name; children: the type arguments.
- `QualifiedTypeNode`: A module-qualified type (`M.Type[T]`). payload: the `NameId` of the type; children: one `TypeQualifierNode`, then the type arguments.
- `TypeQualifierNode`: payload: the `NameId` of the module alias; no children.
- `BoundedTypeNode`: A bounded type argument (`T: Eq + Hash`). payload: the `NameId` of the parameter; children: one `TypeBoundNode` per bound.
- `TypeBoundNode`: payload: the `NameId` of the trait; no children.
- `DimensionNameTypeNode`: A dimension variable (`#N`). payload: the `NameId` of the plain name; no children.
- `VariadicDimensionNameTypeNode`: A variadic dimension variable (`#Ds...`). payload: the `NameId` of the plain name; no children.
- `DimensionWildcardTypeNode`: The wildcard dimension `#_`; no payload or children.
- `VariadicDimensionWildcardTypeNode`: The variadic wildcard dimension `#_...`; no payload or children.
- `DimensionLiteralTypeNode`: A dimension literal (`#3`, or `3` inside a dimension expression). payload: the `LiteralId` of the digits; no children.
- `DimensionAddTypeNode`: children: the left and right dimensions of `+`.
- `DimensionSubtractTypeNode`: children: the left and right dimensions of `-`.
- `DimensionMultiplyTypeNode`: children: the left and right dimensions of `*`.
- `DimensionDivideTypeNode`: children: the left and right dimensions of `/`.
- `RangeTypeNode`: A range type (`..#N`). child: the dimension.
- `TupleTypeNode`: children: the element types.
- `FunctionTypeNode`: An impure function type. children: the parameter types, then the return type last.
- `PureFunctionTypeNode`: A `pure` function type. children: the parameter types, then the return type last.
- `ArrayTypeNode`: A fixed-size array type (`Float[#3]`). children: the element type, then the dimensions.
- `MissingTypeNode`: Where a type was required and none was written; a diagnostic row reports it. No payload or children.
---
enum NodeKind:
	IdentifierNode
	IntegerLiteralNode
	FloatLiteralNode
	StringLiteralNode
	RawStringLiteralNode
	PipeStringLiteralNode
	RawPipeStringLiteralNode
	InterpolatedStringNode
	InterpolationTextNode
	InterpolatedPipeStringNode
	TrueLiteralNode
	FalseLiteralNode
	CharLiteralNode
	NegateNode
	NotNode
